          DIGITAL ONLY PC MANUFACTURER WORLDWIDE TO OFFER
                    COMPLETE WINDOWS 95 SOLUTION


      Systems, Services, Support and Training From One Vendor
        Free Upgrade for PC Purchases Effective Immediately
                                  

MAYNARD, Mass. -- July 11, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it has signed a Windows 95 Operating System 
licensing agreement with Microsoft Corporation.  With this 
agreement, Digital becomes the only PC manufacturer to offer a 
complete Windows 95 solution to corporate customers by providing:

     o	A full range of Windows 95 commercial desktop and notebook 
        PCs that will come pre-loaded with both Windows 95 and 
        Windows for Workgroups, giving users a choice of operating 
        systems on initial boot;

     o	Retail systems shipping pre-loaded with Windows 95 as soon 
        as it is available;

     o	Free Windows 95 upgrades to customers who purchase 
        Digital's commercial (desktop and notebook) or retail PCs 
        between July 1, 1995 and October 1, 1995;

     o	Migration services to help corporate customers move to 
        Windows 95;
 
     o	A full range of technical support for corporate customers; 
        and

     o	Training for both end users and support professionals.

     "Digital and Microsoft have one of the longest and most 
successful working relationships in the industry with Windows and 
Windows NT," said Bernhard Auer, vice president and general manager of 
Digital's Personal Computer Business.  "We are well prepared for this 
major industry transition and have drawn on the Windows experience and 
expertise of many groups within Digital to provide customers with a 
smooth and hassle-free transition to Windows 95." 

     "In our ten years of working together, Digital has been one of 
our strongest Windows supporters," said Bill Gates, CEO of Microsoft 
Corporation.  "They have dedicated more resources than ever before to 
ensure corporate customers experience the easiest possible transition 
to Windows 95."

Dual Install Offers O/S Choice

     To help corporate customers during their migration period, 
Digital will dual-install Microsoft's Windows 95 and Windows for 
Workgroups 3.11/MS-DOS 6.22 on its entire line of professional desktop 
and notebook systems manufactured after Microsoft's release of Windows 
95.  On initial boot, users will be greeted with a welcome screen that 
enables them to select the operating system of choice.  Regardless of 
which operating system is chosen, the software applications that were 
pre-installed at the factory will be automatically configured to the 
appropriate operating system.  These dual-install systems will be 
available through Digital's channel partners.

     "Digital is giving us the flexibility to schedule at our own pace 
our transition from our current Windows environment to Windows 95 for 
both our notebook and desktop systems," said Steve Shoyer, systems 
consultant, Networking Technologies Division at Bank of Boston.  "By 
not locking us into a choice today, we can reap the benefits of 
Windows 95 at our convenience." 

     Digital's retail line of Starion PCs will ship with the Windows 
95 operating system pre-loaded, immediately following release of the 
operating system.  When customers first use their Starion PC, they 
will be able to immediately take advantage of the user-friendly 
operating system.

Limited-Time Free Offer

     Digital also said it will provide a free upgrade to Microsoft's 
Windows 95 operating system, once it is available, to customers who 
purchase Digital's retail or commercial PCs between July 1, 1995 and 
October 1, 1995.

     Customers who buy a Digital desktop or notebook PC during this 
limited-time offer will receive a coupon at the time of purchase 
offering a free upgrade to the Windows 95 operating system.  To 
receive the upgrade, customers need only send the coupon and 
proof-of-purchase to Digital for redemption.  Upgrades will be 
available once the operating system has been released from Microsoft.  

Service, Support and Training

     Digital has a number of worldwide service offerings in place to 
help users before, during and after they transition to Windows 95.  As 
a Worldwide Microsoft Authorized Support Center partner, Digital has 
extensive Microsoft product knowledge, and more than 10 years of 
experience providing third-party support to small, medium and large 
businesses on hardware, software and networking products from more 
than 1,300 vendors.  Digital is one of the companies selected by 
Microsoft to provide telephone support for Windows 95. As part of the 
Microsoft Windows 95 Support Team, Digital will complement Microsoft's 
own product support services by providing telephone support, 
communications and staff resources.

     Digital has more that 15,000 service professionals worldwide, 
including 500 Microsoft Certified Professionals, and 5,000 support 
professionals trained on Microsoft products, including Windows, 
Windows 95, Windows NT and a variety of software application products.  
The company also serves as a worldwide Microsoft Technical Education 
Center.  As the largest Microsoft training partner, Digital has 
trained more than 20,000 customers from corporate to end users on 
Windows, Windows 95 and Windows NT products.

     The company's PCs are backed by a three-year warranty and 
worldwide services and support network, including one year on-site 
service for desktop system and one-year PASSPORT service for 
notebooks.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
