                 DIGITAL ANNOUNCES AVAILABILITY OF 
             INFORMIX/SAP SOLUTION ON ALPHASERVER FAMILY


MAYNARD, Mass. -- July 14, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
announced today a new phase to its long-standing partnerships with 
Informix Software, Inc., of Menlo Park, California, and SAP AG, 
based in Walldorf, Germany, by announcing the availability of a 
powerful new product offering that provides customers with a package 
that combines comprehensive software solutions from both companies 
running on Digital's family of leading-edge AlphaServer systems.   

     This technology alliance represents a significant milestone 
since Digital's AlphaServer family is currently the only platform in 
the industry that has the capability to integrate and fully support 
SAP R/3 business software running on the INFORMIX-OnLine Dynamic 
Server.

     "This technology partnership will be very productive for 
Digital, Informix and SAP AG," said Mike Gallup, vice president of 
Digital's Worldwide Marketing Group. "Each company has unique 
strengths that complement each other, and the alliance demonstrates 
Digital's ability to deliver to our customers a comprehensive 
solution that combines the proven price/performance capabilities of 
the Alpha architecture integrated with offerings from two of the 
industry's premier software companies."

     The well-integrated solution of SAP R/3 operating in concert 
with the parallel-processing strengths of the INFORMIX-OnLine 
database running on Digital's AlphaServer product family provides a 
powerful advantage to customers with high-end applications. 

     Digital's 64-bit AlphaServer line is comprised of systems 
ranging from the main-frame class AlphaServer 8400 enterprise server 
and 8200 departmental SMP server, through the mid-range AlphaServer 
2100 and 2000 SMP models, to the entry-level AlphaServer 1000 and 
400 servers. Digital's AlphaServer 2100, 8400 and 8200 systems all 
run the industry's fastest microprocessor, the Alpha 21164 RISC 
chip.  

     The Informix-SAP-Digital offering has the capability to address 
the most demanding performance requirements, while delivering a 
highly reliable solution for implementations that are mission 
critical in nature.

     "This combination of technology will deliver a highly reliable, 
high speed solution that is capable of handling the most demanding 
mission critical applications," said Steve Sommer, vice president of 
Marketing, Informix.     

     INFORMIX-OnLine is based on the company's next generation, 
parallel processing database architecture known as Dynamic Scalable 
Architecture (DSA). Since the introduction of OnLine Dynamic Server 
in December 1993, Informix has been increasingly considered by many 
industry experts as having the highest performing database in the 
industry. This is especially evident in customer environments 
requiring highly-scalable symmetric multi-processing (SMP) systems.

     Founded in 1972, SAP AG has grown to become one of the largest 
independent software companies in the world and is the market leader 
in standard business software applications. The company, which is 
headquartered in Walldorf, Germany, now employs over 6,300 people. 
In addition to the Walldorf headquarters, SAP is globally 
represented by 26 subsidiaries and affiliates and 6 SAP partner 
companies which collectively maintain offices in more than 40 
countries around the world. With its standard systems, R/2 for 
mainframes and R/3 for client/server platforms, SAP serves more than 
4,500 customers in 50 countries around the world.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
