                   DIGITAL WINS IT CONTRACT FROM THE 
              MINISTRY OF EDUCATION AND TRAINING IN HANOI

     
Hong Kong -- July 5th, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation's 
Vietnam representative office in Hanoi, and its partner, Tecapro 
Company, announced that the Ministry of Education and Training (MOET) 
recently chose Digital to provide information technology equipment to 
secondary schools in all 53 provinces of Vietnam.
     
     MOET has budgeted over 20 billion Vietnamese dong  (approximately
US$1.8 million) for this project.  Tecapro will  provide the personal
computers and the warranty service.   Digital is donating over 100
titles of educational software to  all the secondary schools. 
     
     Dr. Norris Hickerson, Digital Vietnam's General Manager, said, 
"Digital has a long history in education and training and we  are very
pleased that our experience and good reputation has  allowed us to make
great strides in developing relationships  with the educational
institutions in Vietnam.  Last year alone,  Digital trained over 340
thousand customers and employees in  over 140 locations around the
world.
     
     "The use of computers in education has become established in 
Vietnam already, and each year shows an increase in the  facilities
available for students.  Institutions of higher  education have a
particular leadership role to play in the  effective use of computers in
education, and hence in the  development of all aspects of the economy. 
Since 1957,  starting with the Massachusetts Institute of Technology, 
Digital has been a leader of the establishment and improvment  of the
use of IT in education, and we are continuing that work  today in
Vietnam."
     
     According to Michael Davis, General Manager, PC Business, in 
Hanoi, "There was heavy competition for this contract as all  computer
vendors realize the importance of the education market  in the
development of the general IT market in Vietnam.  We are  very proud of
our track record in less than two years of  operations in the country.  
     
     "For example, MOET chose Digital in 1994 as one of four vendors  to
provide IT equipment to universities and Hanoi Polytechnic  University,
the largest technical school, chose Digital to  provide all its IT
equipment.  This year, we are one of two  vendors to provide computers
to the secondary schools  throughout the country."
     
     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated  worldwide
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha   platforms, storage,
networking, software and services, together  with industry-focused
solutions from business partners, help  organizations compete and win in
today's global marketplace. 
