                       DIGITAL NAMES COPPERMAN
                    HEAD OF SYSTEMS BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass, -- July 17, 1995 -- Enrico Pesatori, vice president 
and general manager of Digital Equipment Corporation's Computer 
Systems Division, today appointed Harold D. Copperman, as vice 
president and general manager of the Systems Business Unit (SBU).  
Pesatori has been the acting vice president and general manager of 
the SBU since it was created a year ago.

     The SBU is responsible for developing, manufacturing, 
marketing, selling and supporting Digital's Alpha-based workstations 
and servers, networked solutions and software through partners.     

     "Since joining Digital two years ago, Harry has had a 
significant role in the company's turnaround," said Pesatori.

     "As one of the charter members of the Personal Computer 
Business Unit's senior management team, Harry took a lead role in 
establishing Digital as one of the fastest growing suppliers of 
personal computers so that today our company ranks among the world's 
leaders.  As president of the Americas, he substantially reduced 
operating costs while protecting the revenue base and improving 
gross margins.  And in his most recent position, Harry successfully 
established a strong market presence among our business partners and 
end users for Alpha-based workstations, servers and networked 
software products.  When combined with his engineering background 
and broad experience as a general manager Harry is well suited to 
lead the SBU," continued Pesatori.

     Prior to joining Digital, Copperman, 48, was president and 
Chief Executive Officer of the Information Systems Group of JWP 
Inc.; president and chief operating officer of Commodore Business 
Machines; and vice president and general manager of Eastern 
Operations for Apple Computer.  Copperman also spent 20 years with 
IBM in a range of sales and marketing management positions.  He has 
a bachelor's of science degree in Mechanical Engineering from 
Rutgers University.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
