                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  HELP DESK


OVERVIEW:

As new software technologies are introduced into the client/server 
environment, complex interoperability issues arise.  These can 
impede or even halt the productivity of a workgroup environment--a 
nightmare because of the number of business-critical applications 
being developed in these environments.  Since the cause is rooted in 
the interdependencies of group computing software such as network 
operating systems, electronic mail and customized groupware 
packages, these problems fall to IT managers and help desk 
professionals to solve.

Increasingly, businesses are turning to outside vendors for help 
desk solutions as a way companies can both support their end users 
and save money.  Digital's new Help Desk Services are designed to 
answer this need for cost-effective and responsive support.  
(Department of Defense research points out that a one-minute call to 
a qualified help desk support representative will save the caller, 
on average, seven minutes of self-support.)

The Digital Help Desk now offers both product and problem-solving 
support for the following industry-leading client/server 
technologies:
     

    o  Lotus Notes on multiple platforms--Compaq, Hewlett-Packard, 
       Sun, IBM and Digital's Alpha 

    o  Microsoft Backoffice, including Microsoft Systems Management 
       Server and Windows NT Advanced Server

    o  Digital's POLYCENTER AssetWORKS, an enterprise-wide solution 
       that enables companies to control and manage their software 
       and hardware assets

    o  Multiple network operating systems, including NetWare, Vines, 
       PATHWORKS
       
    o  E-mail systems, such as MS Mail, cc:Mail, and Novell 
       Groupwise

    o  Over 200 Desktop PC applications

Simplified packaging and flexible pricing

In addition to providing advanced support for new client/server 
technologies, Digital also announced a simplified packaging approach 
to help desk support.  Each package varies in the levels of support 
and the kinds of support it provides customers: from PC application 
support to network operating systems (NOS) and client/server 
groupware support.  In addition, a new and more flexible pricing 
approach is now available. This will allow customers to buy support 
the way they want it--per incident, call pack or annual contract.  
This enables companies to tailor their support needs to the way they 
run their businesses.

Each of the new packages--Help Desk Pro, Help Desk Premium and User 
Support Help Desk--provides the right level of help desk support, 
regardless of whether the customer is a help desk professional, LAN 
administrator, system manager or end user. 

Help Desk Pro.  This package is targeted to help desk professionals. 
It provides customers with technical backup support as well as 
support for their desktop applications, NOS/mail products, asset/
system management software.  Customers can purchase the Help Desk 
Pro package on a per incident, call pack or annual contract basis.    

Help Desk Premium.  Aimed at Level II (technical support) staff such 
as LAN and system managers, the Help Desk Premium supports all the 
environments included under Help Desk Pro.  In addition, it 
includes:
        
    o  A faster response time
    o  A named account representative, whose knowledge of a 
       customer's business can play a key role in helping diagnose 
       problems
    o  Remote environment evaluation, for rapid diagnosis

User Support Help Desk.  Digital continues to offer desktop users 
its industry-leading user application support, which provides direct 
advisory support for more than 200 popular PC software applications, 
including Windows 95.

In addition, Digital offers The Custom Help Desk.  This highly 
flexible option is targeted to Level II staff as well as developers.  
Typically aimed at the most complex environments, including 
Groupware environments with numerous customized applications, the 
Custom Help Desk is sold through a statement of work.  Custom Help 
Desk customers, like Help Desk Premium customers, are assigned an 
account representative who works closely with the IT organization to 
keep a site productively running.

Help Desk solutions backed by powerful worldwide capabilities

Digital offers the industry's broadest array of help desk services, 
enabling customers of differing sizes, budgets and needs to meet 
their needs for better performance, improved management of internal 
resources, reduced operating costs and increased customer 
satisfaction. 

Like all of Digital's service and support solutions, help desk 
services benefit from Digital's Multivendor Customer Services' 
worldwide support infrastructure and global presence.  This 
includes:
     
    o  14 fully staffed Customer Support Centers (CSC) worldwide, 24 
       hour/7 day a week support, with broad multivendor hardware, 
       software and networking support

    o  75 percent problem resolution within one hour of the more 
       than 5 million help desk support calls to the CSCs, and 92 
       percent resolution within the same day

    o  More than 30 years experience in supporting mission-critical 
       environments, including more than 12 years of multivendor 
       support

    o  450 worldwide service locations in more than 100 countries

    o  Strategic support alliances with the industry's leading 
       hardware and software companies, including Microsoft, Lotus, 
       Novell, Dell, Oracle, Banyan, SyBase

    o  Full multivendor support for more than 14,000 products

    o  Unparalleled networking expertise in both LANS and WANS

    o  Award-winning service, including:

       -  An "A" rating in PC Magazine's 1995 "Service and 
          Reliability" survey

       -  The 1995 Harold H. Short, Jr., Innovations in Service 
          Award, from Service News, for Digital's recently announced 
          PC Utility, which provides companies with cradle-to-grave 
          technology solutions for every desktop

       -  Five "User's Choice" awards for software service and 
          support from Software Magazine in 1993 in the areas of 
          database, networking and communications, systems 
          management, application development and VAX applications

       -  Three 1993 Digital News & Review "Target Awards" for best 
          overall customer service, best hardware maintenance, and 
          best software support 

Availability and pricing

Digital's newly announced Help Desk Services will be available in 
the US in September. Prices for the various packages, which will be 
sold through and to Digital's business partners, will vary depending 
on package option site configuration.
