                    NEW PATHWORKS SERVER SOFTWARE
                ENERGIZES NOVELL NETWARE ENVIRONMENTS


            ...PATHWORKS for NetWare certified by Novell
             to run on industry-leading Alpha servers...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- July 14, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced new multiplatform support for Novell NetWare users 
with the introduction of PATHWORKS for NetWare on Alpha systems. 
With the availability of the PATHWORKS for NetWare server products 
for the Digital UNIX and OpenVMS platforms, NetWare users can now 
reach out to resources, applications, and information throughout the 
enterprise.

     Co-developed by Digital and Novell and certified by Novell, the 
new PATHWORKS for NetWare servers enable NetWare, OpenVMS and 
Digital UNIX users to share information, applications, disks, 
printers and other resources. With Digital's leadership 64-bit Alpha 
technology, NetWare users gain unprecedented price performance, 
multiprocessing and clustering capabilities on highly reliable and 
scalable servers.

     The new PATHWORKS for NetWare server products provide access to 
server and network resources over Ethernet, Token Ring, and FDDI 
networks using IPX/SPX, LAT, NetBEUI, TELNET, TCP/IP and DECnet 
transports.

     Using DOS and Windows PCs, NetWare users can quickly and easily 
share files, databases, applications, and other information with 
users of Microsoft PC networks, as well as with Macintosh, UNIX 
workstations, and Digital OpenVMS timeshare users. From a single, 
high-performance Alpha server, PATHWORKS for NetWare software 
simultaneously supports multiple network operating systems including 
Novell NetWare, Microsoft LAN Manager, Windows NT and AppleShare.

     Because PC files are stored on Digital servers in native UNIX 
or OpenVMS formats, PATHWORKS for NetWare users can quickly access 
any number and combination of servers, anywhere on the local or wide 
area network. To NetWare clients, the PATHWORKS servers look like 
any other NetWare server. Users continue to use the familiar NetWare 
interface to easily share files and printers on NetWare, Windows NT, 
Windows for Workgroups, IBM LAN Server, LAN Manager and AppleShare 
networks.

     Alpha and VAX PATHWORKS for NetWare servers scale to support 
thousands of active users simultaneously on a single server or 
cluster. PC-based servers can now be consolidated to simplify 
management tasks such as backup and user administration, while 
taking advantage of the advanced availability features of the 
OpenVMS and Digital UNIX operating systems.

     PATHWORKS for Digital UNIX (NetWare) and PATHWORKS for OpenVMS 
(NetWare) products are immediately available. Concurrent user 
pricing ranges from $75 per user for 250 users or more to $300 per 
user for 10 users. Pricing for a single user client license for 
unlimited file and print services is $99. An optional Combined 
Client Server license priced at $205 includes additional features 
such as network administration, the Mosaic Internet browser, 
terminal emulation, workgroup directory services, and X.25, X.32 and 
ISDN connectivity.

     One of the features included in the optional client software is 
the popular ManageWORKS system management application, which can 
manage PATHWORKS for NetWare, native NetWare, LAN Manager and IBM 
LAN Server local area networks from a single Windows PC. Investments 
in NetWare training are protected because NetWare users continue to 
use the same NetWare utilities to manage file and print services on 
the Alpha and VAX servers.

     PATHWORKS for NetWare is a member of Digital's PATHWORKS family 
of networking and network integration solutions for local and wide 
area networks. PATHWORKS integrates the broadest set of PC and 
server platforms with the leading network technologies and network 
operating systems. PATHWORKS solutions are available for all popular 
platforms, including DOS, Windows, Windows NT, Windows for 
Workgroups, NetWare, Macintosh, LAN Manager, UNIX, OpenVMS, OS/2, 
and soon Windows 95.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
                                ####

